  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Policies and programmes developed and implemented to promote and improve safety and health at work</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO is supporting St. Vincent and the Grenadines in developing its occupational safety and health (OSH) system, regulated by the OSH Act adopted in 2017. This includes technical advice for the National OSH Policy and OSH Profile, implementation of the OSH Act, training on OSH inspection, and promoting the ratification of ILO OSH Conventions. The strategy relies on national discussion and ownership, aiming to enhance OSH standards and practices.

The ILO&apos;s support involves technical assistance, expert advice, advocacy, training, and facilitation, guided by ILO Conventions and global best practices. External consultants will assist with interventions, ensuring gender equality and shock responsiveness in OSH. Activities will be coordinated with LABADMIN/OSH, which will provide technical and financial support, and the ITC/ILO may assist with training. This initiative will benefit workers and employers by improving workplace safety and health.</narrative>
  </description>
